WEBVTT

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.430
Here we go.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.650
<i>S2CA Tri-burst!</i>

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:19.260
<i>Gatrandis Babel ziggurat Edenal.</i>

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:26.890
<i>Emustolronzen Finé el Balal zizzl.</i>

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:35.880
<i>Gatrandis Babel ziggurat Edenal.</i>

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:45.690
<i>Emustolronzen Finé el zizzl.</i>

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.360
<i>Superb Song!</i>

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.480
<i>Combination Arts!</i>

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.460
<i>Set Harmonics!</i>

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.730
This is our

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.770
Climax Song!

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.410
What is that crazy thing?!

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:49.710
It's beautiful.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.960
This monster is also our opponent...

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.640
The light of dawn.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:52.750
<b>Episode 3 
Those Who Long for the End, 
Those Who Challenge the End</b>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.110
<i>Superb Song!</i>

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.760
<i>Combination Arts!</i>

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.400
<i>Set Harmonics!</i>

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:09.840
<i>By resonating with another's Climax Song,</i>

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.460
<i>not only does Hibiki amplify its power,</i>

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:17.230
<i>she reduces the stress that occurs 
between wielder and relic.</i>

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.010
<i>The Sakurai Theory says that 
a Climax Song's unique properties</i>

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:24.030
<i>are an extension of the Armed Gear
 the wielder is holding,</i>

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.030
<i>but Tachibana Hibiki's Climax 
Song is clearly intended</i>

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:31.250
<i>to be used when holding another's hands.</i>

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.240
<i>This is the biggest reason that the wielders</i>

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.610
<i>were able to survive, even after using</i>

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.250
<i>their Climax Songs to destroy the 
descending piece of the Moon.</i>

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.760
<i>The trio of Climax Songs created</i>

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.290
<i>an explosive growth in phonic gain,</i>

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.780
<i>which awakened the Nephilim,</i>

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:54.270
<i>the giant that fell from the heavens.</i>

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.880
<i>The heartbeat of awakening...</i>

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:08.250
It's been a week since their declaration 
of war at the concert hall.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:12.120
Yes... It's been a week, 
with nothing happening.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.580
Government sources tell me

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:19.200
there have been no shows of force from 
a terrorist group calling itself Finé,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.570
or, indeed, any negotiations at all.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.240
In other words,

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:28.340
we have no idea in the slightest what they want.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.770
At first glance,

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:33.600
that flashy performance appears only to be 
intended to let the world know they exist.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.310
Thanks to that, Section 2 was able 
to respond quickly, but...

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:42.020
If they have some grand plot,
this is a strange way to go about it.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.810
It might be that's exactly what they intended.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.040
Commander Kazanari.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.370
<b>Duty</b>

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.370
Ogawa? What's going on there?

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:54.390
I've been tracing the trailer we found abandoned

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:53.540
I don't know who you think you are, bastard,

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.370
but you aren't making it out alive...

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.370
near the concert hall.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:57.760
Get him!

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.890
I tracked it back to a construction company,

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:04.050
whose books showed large purchases 
of medical equipment,

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:07.970
pharmaceuticals, and measuring devices 
from a fictional company.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.340
Medical devices?

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.280
It would've been about two months ago.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.600
The people here were using it as

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.290
a form of money laundering, but...

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.360
Don't these records interest you?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.940
Sounds like it'll be worth pursuing.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.880
<i>There are two Gungnir Symphogears...</i>

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.390
<i>Then it makes sense that we'd both 
have our own reasons to fight.</i>

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.680
I just want to help people in trouble!

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.600
That's why...

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.940
That's what I mean by hypocrisy.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:08.580
<i>The reason I fight...</i>

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:12.340
<i>I'm not lying to myself...</i>

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.330
Hibiki! Hibiki!

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.270
Tachibana-san, is something bothering you?

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.080
Yeah, something very important...

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.780
It's fall, right?

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:29.920
I'm sure you have many things going on.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.510
Things more important than my class, for example.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:36.430
Huh?

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.650
We've moved to this new building, and we 
have a festival coming up in three days.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:45.010
Everyone is enjoying a new life, 
in a new environment.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:48.070
And you haven't changed a bit. You're always...

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.980
Always, always, always, always...

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.480
B-But, Sensei, I may not be 
the most attentive person,

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:59.870
but I actually have dear friends 
that want me not to change.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:00.950
Tachibana-san!

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.690
Dummy.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:10.210
And what I couldn't believe is that

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.470
they just poured it on the rice!

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.340
Isn't that weird?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.950
And then...

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:24.230
Are you still thinking about her?

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.610
If we talk, we can understand each other!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.980
We don't have to...

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:33.910
I refuse to accept that someone 
who bears no burdens

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.860
is the hero that saved humanity.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:37.720
Yeah.

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:41.090
If there's something you really have to do,

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:43.120
you have to bear that burden,

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.030
even if you know it's wrong...

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:52.420
If she's supposed to save people, then why?

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:18.470
Even so, we must

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.990
get along with our own sense of what is right.

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.410
We have no time left

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.500
for turning back or hesitating.

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:30.400
Maria...

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:49.380
<i>That is the starvation impulse, spoken of in legend,</i>

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.970
<i>that will cause it to eat even its own kind...</i>

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.900
<i>Controlling the Nephilim is beyond human power.</i>

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:59.510
Please don't think of them as an 
ancient civilization's legacy,

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.160
beyond our power to control.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.110
Dr. Ver...

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.730
Even if they are beyond human power to control,

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:11.670
if they can be controlled by 
a hero, isn't that enough?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.700
Mom! What was that alarm?

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.930
The next flower is still a bud,

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.050
and must be treated carefully.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.880
You were worried about me, huh?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.390
But it's okay.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.930
The Nephilim was thrashing about, that's all.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.790
I lowered the bulkheads and fed it.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:31.600
It should calm itself soon.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:35.860
Mom...

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.310
The appropriate steps have been taken. It's fine.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:42.470
More importantly, isn't it time for your inspection?

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.330
Frontier is this plan's other critical aspect.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.090
I cannot miss the inspections

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:51.130
before it's activated, but...

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.570
Don't worry about this.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:55.000
While you're gone,

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.510
I'll get the Nephilim some more food.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:02.160
I'll have Shirabe and Kirika guard you.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.170
I'm not planning on any fights, so I'll be fine.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:08.520
Wouldn't it be better to focus 
our forces on your side?

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:11.570
Understood.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:14.200
I'll return at the appointed time.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.440
Please take care of the rest.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:29.410
<i>Now, will my prey come for the bait I've laid?</i>

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:46.950
I can't say I approve of failure to pay attention

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:48.640
when running in the hallways...

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.790
Ow!

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:54.730
Yukine? What's the hurry?

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:57.720
They... They're chasing me.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:59.570
They're almost here!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.550
What?

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.620
I don't see anyone suspicious.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.070
Okay...

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:09.040
Guess I lost them.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.800
Who are "they"?

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:15.110
The people in my class,

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:19.300
who keep trying to get me 
involved in this school stuff.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.100
Yukine-san!

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.300
Jeez, where did she go?

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:29.060
Those weird Finé guys are running around.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.030
We don't have time...

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:33.230
What are you doing?

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.050
Just what it looks like.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:38.320
Preparing for that "school stuff" 
you're about to be involved in.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:42.190
<b>Fall Cherry Blossom Fair</b>

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.200
<b>Fall Cherry Blossom Fair</b>

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.240
I guess I'll have you help me, as well, Yukine!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.950
<b>03 Days Until the Fall Cherry Blossom Fair</b>

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:50.950
Why?

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.980
When you head back, they'll make 
you do it, anyway.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.460
So you can help me a little, right?

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.950
You still aren't used to this lifestyle?

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:12.070
I don't want to hear it from someone 
who isn't used to it at all.

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.620
That's true.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.640
But you know, Yukine...

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.730
Oh, Tsubasa-san! There you are.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.480
You went to get supplies and didn't return,

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.980
so everyone's been looking for you.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.130
But I guess we shouldn't have worried.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:27.160
You have a cute underclassman with you.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:29.490
I thought you'd all gone home already.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.570
Well, you seem to think 
it's your fault that preparations

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:34.610
for the school fair are behind.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:36.750
So we want to help!

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:39.300
You want to help?

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.370
Hey, you're pretty popular!

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:47.260
But it's true that you used to be 
a little tough to approach...

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.440
That's right.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:51.690
"The solitary diva" sounds cool, but...

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:53.080
But at first, it seemed

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:56.020
like you were part of a different world.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:59.080
Well, she's a celebrity and a top artist.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.170
But you know...

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:00.770
Yeah.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.170
When we actually talked to you,

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.710
we realized you're just like us!

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:07.280
Everyone...

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.910
Especially lately.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:14.950
Heh, you're getting along well!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.150
I'm sorry. Did that upset you?

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.170
I don't know.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:19.950
But maybe I should

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:23.170
try a little harder, too...

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.420
I see.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:28.190
Let's do a little more work, okay?

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.400
Right, let's finish this up!

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:38.560
Listen, be ready to end this tonight!

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.690
I'm sorry to make you come out

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.320
this late on a school night.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.120
Don't worry about it.

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:47.570
As protectors, this is our job.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.820
I can't believe they were hiding just outside town...

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:55.580
This hospital was shut down a long time ago.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.580
But it looks like they've been bringing in supplies,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.830
bit by bit, for the past two months.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:05.340
But I hate to say that, at the moment, that's all the information we have.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:07.590
If they won't come out of their hole,

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.010
we'll just have to drag them out!

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.980
The Symphogear-wielders are 
heading inside the building.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.650
Let's give them a warm welcome.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:41.620
It sure feels like an abandoned hospital, doesn't it?

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.680
What, are you scared?

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:45.000
That isn't it!

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.340
The air just feels heavy...

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.840
They're coming after us surprisingly quickly.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:16:02.310
<i>Killiter Ichaival tron.</i>

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.720
Bang!

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:37.470
<i>A Gatling gun has no need for greetings.</i>

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.720
<i>Disparity's heading for the trash bin.</i>

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:43.230
<i>One, two, three! Get out of my sight...</i>

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:47.040
<i>If you want me to blow a hole in you,</i>

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:47.630
I knew it. These Noise...

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.650
<i>get in line and say, "Adios."</i>

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:49.650
Yeah, they're being controlled.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:53.570
<i>One, two, three! Get out of my face...</i>

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:53.040
Tachibana, cover Yukine!

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.280
Make sure they don't get near her!

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:56.530
<i>Feelings burned into hot metal,</i>

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:55.950
Right!

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:59.080
<i>for the warm ties that bind me.</i>

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.500
<i>This stuff ain't my style,</i>

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:02.630
Take this!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.540
<i>but I don't mind...</i>

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:07.920
<i>Be a good kid, and go the hell to bed.</i>

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:12.920
<i>Ha ha! Go to Hell! It's super confession time!</i>

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:17.630
<i>Go kneel and beg before Satan, in the pits of Hell.</i>

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:22.790
<i>Ha ha! Go to Hell! I won't regret anymore!</i>

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:27.570
<i>I have a place to protect now,</i>

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.440
<b>Azure Flash</b>

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:31.530
<i>so I won't run anymore!</i>

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:42.660
Why is this so hard?

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.170
Our Gear output is dropping!

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:49.970
The wielder's compatibility values are dropping!

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.670
At this rate, they won't be able 
to continue the battle!

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.420
What's going on?

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.970
Watch out, both of you!

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:12.440
We hit that thing with an Armed Gear!

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.690
Why isn't the carbon shattering?

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:17.700
Is it not a Noise?

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.300
Then what is that monster?

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:31.750
Dr. Ver?

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.130
You're smarter than I thought.

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:43.360
But you disappeared during the 
attack on the Iwakuni base!

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:46.270
Then all the Noise attacks...

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:49.480
To tell the truth, it was a simple trick.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.890
When you last saw me,

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:53.660
the Staff of Solomon wasn't even in the case.

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.680
It was hidden inside my coat.

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:01.880
Then you controlled the Noise and pretended 
that they were attacking you,

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.120
so you could steal the Staff of Solomon?

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:09.670
This staff is the only thing capable 
of summoning Noise

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.400
from the Treasury of Babylonia 
and controlling them.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.600
And I am the only one

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:19.820
who is fit to wield it.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.970
Don't you think?

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.050
Hell, no!

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:43.630
Compatibility values are dropping,

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:46.330
and the Gear-backfire is devouring the wielders!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:52.990
Damn it...

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.600
Why am I the one who's taking damage?

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.300
<i>If we use our powerful attacks 
in this situation,</i>

00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:04.730
<i>the backfire could kill us in the worst case.</i>

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:06.640
<i>What's that?</i>

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:12.020
The Noise are taking that cage away?!

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.720
It's going out to sea!

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:21.660
<i>Now that I'm not carrying so much,</i>

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.490
<i>I'd love to get some more data...</i>

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:32.700
Tachibana, capture him! And take care of Yukine!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.940
<i>With the Ame no Habakiri's mobility, 
I should be able to...</i>

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:44.510
Tsubasa-san is catching up to 
the escaping Noise, but...

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:45.640
<i>If you fear monsters,</i>

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:45.640
Commander!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.640
<i>that is but a mirror held up to your own weakness.</i>

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.640
Just jump, Tsubasa!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.660
<i>If I don't do it, who will?</i>

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:51.310
<i>Jump?</i>

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.140
Jump straight out, over the sea.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:56.900
<i>Awaken, invincible azure warrior that slays evil!</i>

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.840
No matter what, you are...

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:00.480
<i>Thousands, millions, billions of lives...</i>

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:03.450
<i>I'll hold them close, as I swing my blade.</i>

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.580
<i>A flash of destruction that 
makes your blood run cold.</i>

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.280
Temporary HQ, emergency surface!

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.540
<i>Are you prepared to die?</i>

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:12.680
<i>Tonight, the crescent Moon is in the sky,</i>

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:15.770
<i>like a killing blade.</i>

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:25.180
<i>Now vanish beneath the flames of my blade!</i>

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.560
Tsubasa-san?

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.360
That's...

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.910
Right on time, Finé.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:50.120
Finé?

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.480
The name which signifies the end is 
the symbol of our organization,

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:56.500
and also her second name.

00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:59.750
No way... Then she's...

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:04.760
The newly awakened second coming of Finé!
